{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nCommit 1d75850974 (ticket f124, 'close the ambient-default provider leak') landed ~10 minutes after the comment-hygiene gate itself (f2b2d0b410, ticket b047) via concurrent Gerrit review — its comments cite a bare GitHub Actions run id three times, which the new whole-tree gate rejects. Every change pushed after 1d75850974 now fails CI's lint job (observed: change 1309 ps4, change 1311 ps3), i.e. main is red for everyone.\n\n## Approach\nReplace the three bare run-id citations with durable prose citing ticket f124 (the incident's ticket, per the gate's own teaching message. Sites: tests/external/test_provider_matrix_live.py:56, tests/unit/test_ci_provider_matrix.py:22, tests/unit/test_ci_provider_matrix.py:157.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py exits 0 on the tree\n- [x] the three comments still convey the same incident evidence (provider leak shipped while class-only assertion passed), now citing f124"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785790520341831001,"uuid":"814a9091-5c96-4ef7-aa5c-9282b06e8b9e"}